# Patterns excluded from the semantic-test comparison report.
#
# Format: one POSIX ERE pattern per line. Lines starting with '#' and blank
# lines are treated as documentation and stripped by compare_test_results.sh
# before being passed to grep -f (which otherwise parses every non-empty
# line, including comments, as a regex).
#
# Patterns MUST be valid POSIX ERE so the filter works identically on BSD
# grep (macOS) and GNU grep (Linux). In particular: use [[:space:]] not \s,
# and [[:space:]][[:space:]]* not \s+ .
-att[0-9]*-
^[0-9]*c[0-9]*
^[0-9]*,[0-9]*c[0-9]*,[0-9]*
---
ClioInput[[:space:]]-[[:space:]]version
KleioTranslator\ -\ server\ version
<KLEIO STRUCTURE="
CLASS="relation"
-rel[0-9]*-
translations=[0-9]*
Processing data file
Translation count:
Processed file-
Original file-
Previous version-
Temp file with ids-
[0-9]*-[0-9]*-[0-9]*[[:space:]][0-9]*-[0-9]*
Current time:
<ELEMENT NAME="order" CLASS="order"><core>[0-9]*</core></ELEMENT>
<core><!\[CDATA\[[A-Za-z0-9\/\._\-]*reference_translations/
<core><!\[CDATA\[[A-Za-z0-9\/\._\-]*test_translations/
# Source-path echo lines (leading whitespace plus path). The original patterns
# used negative-lookahead PCRE syntax, which is invalid in ERE and made
# grep -E abort the whole filter run (silently dumping the unfiltered diff).
# Rewritten in ERE: require leading whitespace, which inherently excludes the
# diff -r and Only in headers (those start at column 0).
^[[:space:]][[:space:]]*[A-Za-z0-9/\._\-]*reference_translations/
^[[:space:]][[:space:]]*[A-Za-z0-9/\._\-]*test_translations/
^[[:space:]][[:space:]]*reference_translations
^[[:space:]][[:space:]]*test_translations
# WARNING:/ERROR: lines that differ only by absolute vs relative .cli path.
# Stable emits a bare relative filename like 'WARNING: obiteirasproblem.cli
# line 33 ...', the dev translator emits an absolute path under
# .../test_translations/. The error/warning content after the path is
# identical, so these are path-format differences only. Filter both sides:
# the > side by its absolute test_translations path, the < side by a bare
# relative filename with no '/' before .cli so the paired hunk disappears.
^[<>][[:space:]]*(WARNING|ERROR):[[:space:]].*test_translations/
^[<][[:space:]]*(WARNING|ERROR):[[:space:]][A-Za-z0-9._-]+\.cli[[:space:]]
ID="[A-Za-z0-9\.\-]*-[a-z0-9]*"
# <ELEMENT NAME
<ELEMENT NAME="id"\ CLASS="id"><core>[A-Za-z0-9\ \.\-]*-[a-z0-9]*<\/core><\/ELEMENT>
# Element *declaration* lines (no <core> content) whose only stable/dev
# difference is in the SUPER_CLASS / BASE_CLASS attributes. These are derived
# schema metadata, not source-document content. The char class includes 0-9_
# so data-type values match (string256, string64, ...). The full-line anchor
# (note the trailing >) avoids matching element lines that carry <core> data.
#
# This hides the BASE_CLASS divergence between the stable engine and the dev
# engine (issue #58): the dev clio_element_bclass/2 returns the element's own
# class as BASE_CLASS (abstract data types skipped), while stable returns the
# chain root. Verified across all test files that, for every line matched here,
# the CLASS attribute is identical on both sides - so no genuine CLASS
# regression is being hidden. This is plumbing work tracked in
# NEXT_STEPS.md (Priority 6); remove this line once the importer is verified
# and the bclass logic is back-ported to stable.
# Caveat: a genuinely-wrong SUPER_CLASS would not be flagged here, but would
# still surface via the element's TYPE=/SIZE= and <core> length lines.
^[<>-][[:space:]]*<ELEMENT NAME="[a-z0-9_]*"\ SUPER_CLASS="[a-z0-9_]*"\ BASE_CLASS="[a-z0-9_]*"\ CLASS="[a-z0-9_]*">[[:space:]]*$
TYPE="varchar"\ SIZE="[0-9]*"
"kleio_file":
"kleio_original":
"kleio_previous":
"kleio_rpt":
"stru":
"stru_json":
"stru_rpt":
# Structure error/warning counts: emitted only by the dev (YAML) translator's
# .files.json. The stable translator does not emit these keys. The warnings
# currently reflect known duplicate include:/group-definition issues in the
# YAML structures (tracked separately); filtering the count lines here keeps
# them out of the comparison report. Remove these if those counts should
# become part of the regression signal.
"stru_errors":
"stru_warnings":
Groups in this file:
Elements in this file:
Structure file:
Local structure file: 
Structure processing report:
Structure in JSON:
Structure file:
Structure processing report:
Structure in JSON: 
Kleio file:
Original file:
Previous version:
Temp file with ids:
-renamed to-
# Timestamps in .err/.rpt files (YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS)
[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9][[:space:]][0-9][0-9]:[0-9][0-9]:[0-9][0-9]
# Header format differences between stable and dev translators
# Note: stable emits 'Structure: <file>', dev emits 'Declared structure: <file>'
# plus a 'Used structure: <abs-path>' line. These are cosmetic report-format
# differences, not translation differences. Match any .str/.yaml filename.
^< Structure: [a-zA-Z0-9_./-]+\.(str|yaml)$
^> Declared structure: [a-zA-Z0-9_./-]+\.(str|yaml)$
^> Used structure:
# Extra blank lines introduced by dev header format
^> $
# Diff add/delete markers left after content filtering
^[0-9]*a[0-9]*$
^[0-9]*d[0-9]*$